From 294181a2c627984a69c438f6cad82154251d9e90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linuxopt <305337987+linuxopt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:51:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Name entry: Japanese (and any language) typed, pasted or from
 an input method

The game's name entry took ASCII only with a controller, counted bytes (a
Japanese character is 3: names were cut inside a character), had no
Japanese glyphs and pasted only from ImGui's own clipboard.
- characters counted, cut and deleted whole (runtime/utf8_text.c)
- Noto Sans JP's kana and common kanji merged into the big font the first
  time the name entry opens (the game's Japanese heading shows too)
- Ctrl+V / Shift+Insert paste the system clipboard; an input method's
  candidate window is placed at the field
- the game's starting name kept in UTF-8, not '?'

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
